{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/616628-how-to-run-an-arcadia-chronicle","id":616628,"title":"How to Run an Arcadia Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-05T10:10:31-07:00","id":616628,"title":"How to Run an Arcadia Chronicle","content":"Due to a particular setting catching my interest, I've been tossing the idea of an Arcadia chronicle (for CtL1e) about--one where the twofold goal of the player characters is to grab hold of enough inklings of identity or visions of the <s>Surface</s> real world to make escaping possible and then to create and execute a plan for doing it.<br /> <br /> My question is, how would creation change for such a game? Things I've already thought of include eliminating Clarity altogether, and asking my players to build their characters as they are now, leaving their human identities for me and my co-ST to work out and surprise them with. Thoughts, ideas, comments, concerns?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:08:58-07:00","id":616678,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't really think there'd be a lot of changes. I'd say keep Clarity, and have it function like Memory in Mummy. Have breaking points that raises it. The higher it rises, the more of reality you remember.<br /> <br /> You'd need to have some kind of rule on how people look - its hard to have a game when someone is a bubbling river and another is trapped on a wick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}